  "title": "Kirby Problem 4.75",
  "statement": {
    "representation": "markdown-latex",
    "text": "Let X be a connected smooth 4-manifold with nonempty boundary, with finite $\\pi_{1}(X)$, and let $k \\geq$ 0. Let $Diff_{\\partial}(X)$ denote the group of diffeomorphisms of X that are the identity near $\\partial X$. Is the image of the natural map $s_{*}: \\pi_{k}(Diff_{\\partial}(X)) \\to$ colim $\\pi_{k}(Diff_{\\partial}(X\\#_{N}S^{2} \\times S^{2}))$ (11) $N \\to \\infty$ finitely generated? What about the analogous problem in the topological category?",
